From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 02:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 394/394] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali: let the CPU bandwidth
 monitors vote for LLCC

The two CPU bandwidth monitors (cluster 0 at 0x310b3400, cluster 1 at
0x310b7400) count the CPU clusters' traffic into the GEM NoC, LLCC hits
included, but vote that bandwidth on the CPU -> DDR path. A cache-bound
workload therefore raises the DDR clock it does not use.

Stock canoe does it differently: its bwmon-llcc-gold / bwmon-llcc-prime
instances at the same two addresses target the LLCC DCVS device (16-byte
bus width, llcc-freq-table 282-1350 MHz), and DDR follows from the LLCC
monitor (bwmon-ddr at 0x31091000, which this tree already describes as
the LLCC -> DDR monitor) and from the secondary LLCC -> DDR map. SM8650
upstream also votes CPU -> LLCC from these monitors.

Vote gem_noc MASTER_APPSS_PROC -> gem_noc SLAVE_LLCC and give the shared
OPP table stock's nine LLCC levels as kBps (kHz x 16): 4512000 to
21600000. The LLCC -> DDR monitor and the memory-latency governor (SCMI
memlat on the CPUCP) keep voting DDR as before.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi | 30 +++++++++----------------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
index 82283a7842a5..a8d71df8577c 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali.dtsi
@@ -7884,7 +7884,7 @@ pmu@310b3400 {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 581 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 			interconnects = <&gem_noc MASTER_APPSS_PROC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY
-					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
+					 &gem_noc SLAVE_LLCC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
 
 			operating-points-v2 = <&cpu_bwmon_opp_table>;
 
@@ -7892,47 +7892,39 @@ cpu_bwmon_opp_table: opp-table {
 				compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
 				opp-0 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <2188000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <4512000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-1 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <5412000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <5600000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-2 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <6220000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <8528000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-3 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <6832000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <9689600>;
 				};
 
 				opp-4 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <8368000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <12896000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-5 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <10944000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <14928000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-6 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <12748000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <17056000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-7 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <14744000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <19376000>;
 				};
 
 				opp-8 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <16896000>;
-				};
-
-				opp-9 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <19120000>;
-				};
-
-				opp-10 {
-					opp-peak-kBps = <21332000>;
+					opp-peak-kBps = <21600000>;
 				};
 			};
 		};
@@ -7945,7 +7937,7 @@ pmu@310b7400 {
 			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 581 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 			interconnects = <&gem_noc MASTER_APPSS_PROC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY
-					 &mc_virt SLAVE_EBI1 QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
+					 &gem_noc SLAVE_LLCC QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>;
 
 			operating-points-v2 = <&cpu_bwmon_opp_table>;
 		};
